<title>FINLAND: VALMET TO CUT AIR SYSTEMS STAFF BELOW 500.</title>
<headline>VALMET TO CUT AIR SYSTEMS STAFF BELOW 500.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Valmet Oy said in a statement on Friday it would cut staff at its Turku air systems unit to below 500 from the current 630 people by the end of 1997.  </p>
<p>&quot;Valmet plans to reduce the production of air systems in Turku so that the number of staff will be reduced from current 630 to below 500 by the end of 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The profitability and competitiveness of air systems production will be secured by adjustment and streamlining of operations and by increasing sub-contractor flexibility, Valmet said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 -9 - 680 50 240</p>
